Maya: FYI: We're rolling a deprecation notice for model rdw-embed-1 -> rdw-embed-2. rdw-embed-2 has 1536 dims; old was 1024. Docs need a migration snippet & a compatibility note about embedding dimension mismatches. Need a tiny code example on client-side handling and guidance for vector DB owners. cc @Sam @Ben
Sam: ack. I can draft a PR for the migration guide. Do we want to include automatic up/down-sampling snippet or recommend recomputing embeddings?
Ben: strongly prefer recommending recompute. Downsampling loses quality. But include a small fallback example for quick rollouts.
Alex: note — search-indexes with 1024 dims will break if callers start sending 1536 vectors. We should add a clear "breaking change" banner + recommended steps for customers with minimal infra.
Maya: good. Plan for docs PR: 1) Breaking-change banner + timeline, 2) migration steps (recompute vs adapter), 3) code snippet for adapter + warning, 4) redirect/alias map note for model aliases, 5) cross-link to SDK release notes.
Sam: I'll open a draft PR shortly. Who owns the example code? @Ben?
Ben: happy to write example. Proposed snippet (js) below:
```js
// quick adapter: trim/pad vector to 1536 for ingestion (not recommended long-term)
function adaptEmbedding(vec, targetDim) {
  if (vec.length === targetDim) return vec;
  if (vec.length > targetDim) return vec.slice(0, targetDim);
  // pad with zeros
  return vec.concat(new Array(targetDim - vec.length).fill(0));
}
```
Maya: include an explicit note above the snippet: "This adapter is an emergency compatibility shim only — recompute is recommended." Also add a short Python snippet for clients:
```py
def adapt_embedding(vec, target_dim=1536):
    if len(vec) == target_dim:
        return vec
    if len(vec) > target_dim:
        return vec[:target_dim]
    return vec + [0.0] * (target_dim - len(vec))
```
Sam: I added a TODO in the PR to ask Eng to add a runtime warning in the SDK when dims mismatch. @Alex can you own the SDK warning?
Alex: can do. Will add a deprecation warning that triggers when the model alias resolves to a model with dim != stored vectors.
Maya: timeline: draft PR by EOD, review by eng/docs, merge by Wed next week, coordinated tweet/email deprecation notice on Thu. Also update the model catalog page.
